, \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.04730\", \"title\": \"Understanding Black-box Predictions via Influence Functions\", \"venue\": \"\", \"year\": 2017}\n\n{\"citation_count\": null, \"citation_key\": \"Broderick2020Automatic\", \"id\": \"ref.starter.Broderick2020Automatic\", \"paper_id\": null, \"query\": \"task-brief starter literature (title, venue and year as listed in the task brief)\", \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-10-28T22:00:00+00:00\", \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.14999\", \"title\": \"An Automatic Finite-Sample Robustness Metric: When Can Dropping a Little Data Make a Big Difference?\", \"venue\": \"\", \"year\": 2020}\n\n{\"citation_count\": null, \"citation_key\": \"Min2025Rigging\", \"id\": \"ref.starter.Min2025Rigging\", \"paper_id\": null, \"query\": \"task-brief starter literature (title, venue and year as listed in the task brief)\", \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-10-28T22:00:00+00:00\", \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.17858\", \"title\": \"Improving Your Model Ranking on Chatbot Arena by Vote Rigging\", \"venue\": \"\", \"year\": 2025}\n\n{\"citation_count\": null, \"citation_key\": \"Singh2025Illusion\", \"id\": \"ref.starter.Singh2025Illusion\", \"paper_id\": null, \"query\": \"task-brief starter literature (title, venue and year as listed in the task brief)\", \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-10-28T22:00:00+00:00\", \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.20879\", \"title\": \"The Leaderboard Illusion\", \"venue\": \"\", \"year\": 2025}\n\npaper_evidence_audit_packet.md:632:\\citet{Chiang2024Chatbot} describe the Chatbot Arena platform, in which users vote between two anonymous model responses and the votes are aggregated into rankings. \\citet{Min2025Rigging} study strategies by which votes on such platforms can be manipulated to change rankings, and \\citet{Singh2025Illusion} analyse evaluation practices on the same platform, including private testing and differences in data access and sampling across providers. \\citet{Zheng2023Judging} release expert human and GPT-4 pairwise judgments on MT-Bench. We use the Arena and MT-Bench comparison data, but our attack is a generic, evaluator-verified probe; we do not model any platform's actual voting interface or an adversary's access to it.\n38:Treat the run history as private evidence used to synthesize a clean scientific narrative.\n80:7. Singh, S. et al. (2025). The Leaderboard Illusion. https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.20879 （2025-04-29）。说明：分析 Chatbot Arena 的评测实践（如私有测试、不同提供方的数据访问与采样差异）及其对排行榜的影响。\n244:Use recent memory only as private planning context. It must not determine the visible structure of the paper. The paper should still read like a self-contained scientific paper.\n279:- Install auxiliary tools and libraries in a private directory under `$TMPDIR`, outside the manuscript workspace. Keep package trees and their symlinks out of the paper directory; they prevent safe resume.\n404:Before writing the abstract, privately sketch the broad context, the concrete setting, the exact gap or question, the central method or hypothesis, the strongest grounded result, the strongest comparison point, and the broader implication or main limit. Then write the abstract from that private plan rather than from the order in which the run unfolded. The closing portion of the abstract can use one or two sentences to place the results in a more general context and, when accessibility is materially improved, may also add two or three sentences that provide a broader perspective readable to a scientist in any discipline.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f913bc74-aaf7-49db-a436-770fdb932282","uuid":"e14f84ae-6110-4f67-9c5a-aed31be6819b","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:54:33.723Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"citation_count\": 51, \"citation_key\": \"Gao2021UncertaintyQI\", \"id\": \"ref.s2.b65b46292745d2301a8464eb8c50fe716086fd1e\", \"paper_id\": \"b65b46292745d2301a8464eb8c50fe716086fd1e\", \"query\": \"Bradley-Terry model pair